# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the ONLY secrets mechanism in this repo is
# inventory/group_vars/aap/secrets.yml, which is VAULT-ENCRYPTED AND COMMITTED.
# One file, both environments. Credentials only; hostnames and API URLs live in
# the committed plaintext group_vars/<env>/connection.yml.
#
# secrets.yml is deliberately NOT ignored — it is meant to be tracked. What
# stops a plaintext one being committed is utilities/check-no-secrets.sh, which
# fails the build if a tracked secrets.yml does not start with $ANSIBLE_VAULT.
# That check is the safety net; do not remove it.
#
# The vault PASSWORD is the one secret that cannot be vaulted. It lives outside
# this repo at ~/secrets/.vault_pass_sales_demos (chmod 600, chmod 700 dir).
# The patterns below are belt-and-braces in case one is ever copied in here.
#
# Do NOT add a second sourceable secrets file (no docs/dev-environment.sh).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vault_pass
.vault_pass*
.vault_password
*.vault_pass
*.vault-password
.vault-password

# Kubeconfigs and cluster credentials
**/kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform — state can contain secrets in plaintext; tfvars almost always do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ansible — collections are NEVER vendored into this repo. They install to the
# recommended path (Ansible's default ~/.ansible/collections) from the pinned
# collections/requirements.yml. Two artifact directories get created here and
# neither belongs in git:
#
#   collections/ansible_collections/  ansible-galaxy, if pointed at the repo
#   .ansible/                         ansible-lint's generated module mocks
#
# The .ansible/ mocks are regenerated from .ansible-lint `mock_modules` on
# every run, so tracking them only guarantees they go stale. (#8)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.retry
collections/ansible_collections/
!collections/requirements.yml
.ansible/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
